{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"e2df3fa5348a15157c7c0abc8a10eeca2dfad0d635023626bff644b51ae5b8da","packTokens":2535,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":281,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":2,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":2116,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build a three-screen web portal for parts ordering (Find parts, Cart, My orders)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Display parts with search and filtering by category and brand\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement shopping cart with add/remove/quantity management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Build checkout with delivery address and option selection\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Create order placement and order history tracking\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Support order cancellation and status timeline visualization\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Ensure WCAG 2.1 AA compliance and responsive design\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Deliver 2-second page load performance with 5,000 parts\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The portal provides exactly three screens for a signed-in buyer: Find parts at /parts, Cart and checkout at /cart, and My orders at /orders, with order details shown on the same /orders page.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Each screen's header links to the other two screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"The parts API returns parts sorted alphabetically by name, 20 per page, with image, name, part number, brand, price (GBP, 2 decimals), and stock state.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Stock state is 'In stock' for 5 or more, 'Low stock (n left)' for 1 to 4, and 'Out of stock' for 0.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"When search text has at least 2 characters, the parts API filters by name or part number, case-insensitively.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Category and brand filters restrict results to the chosen single category and brand, combined with search text, with 'All' meaning no filter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Changing search text or a filter on Find parts resets the view to page 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"When no parts match, the portal shows 'No parts match' with a button that clears the search and filters and shows page 1 of all parts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Pressing 'Add to cart' on an in-stock part adds a new line with quantity 1 or increases an existing line's quantity by 1, up to available stock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"The header shows a live cart count equal to the sum of all line quantities, updating without reload.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"The 'Add to cart' button is disabled for out-of-stock parts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Each cart line shows name, part number, unit price, quantity, and line total (unit price times quantity).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Changing a line's quantity recalculates that line's total and the overall order totals immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Invalid quantities (blank, 0, above 99, or non-whole numbers) are corrected to the nearest whole number from 1 to 99.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Quantities above available stock are capped to the stock amount with a message 'Only n available'.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Pressing 'Remove' on a cart line deletes that line.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Cart lines are stored in browser local storage keyed to the buyer's ID so the cart persists across reloads on the same device, without leaking between buyers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"An empty cart shows 'Your cart is empty' with a link to Find parts and hides checkout controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"'Place order' is enabled only when the address is 5 to 200 characters and a delivery option (Standard or Next day) is chosen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Checkout shows subtotal, delivery charge (Standard £0.00, Next day £9.99), and total as subtotal plus delivery charge.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Placing a valid order saves it with status Placed, a sequential order number formatted ORD-NNNNNN, each line's current part price as unit price, and total as subtotal plus delivery charge.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Orders with no lines, invalid quantities, unknown part numbers, invalid addresses, or missing/unknown delivery options are rejected with status 400 and not saved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Orders with any line quantity exceeding available stock are rejected with status 409, returning affected part numbers with available stock, and are not saved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"After a successful order, the portal empties the cart and displays the new order number.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"If placing an order fails due to a network or server error, the portal shows an error message and retains the cart lines, address, and delivery option.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Placing or cancelling an order never changes the part's stock quantity in the parts database.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"Requests without a valid session are rejected with status 401.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"The buyer ID used for orders comes from the session, not the request body.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"The orders API returns only the requesting buyer's own orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"Orders are returned newest first, each with order number, date placed, item count, total, and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"A status filter on My orders restricts results to that buyer's orders with the chosen status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"Opening an order returns its lines (part number, name, quantity, unit price), delivery address, delivery option, total, and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"The order detail shows a status timeline (Placed, Packed, Dispatched, Delivered) with the current status marked by text as well as colour.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"A 'Cancel order' button with confirmation is shown only while an order's status is Placed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"Confirming cancellation on a Placed order sets its status to Cancelled via the API.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"If the order is no longer Placed when cancellation is confirmed, the API refuses with status 409, leaves the status unchanged, and the portal shows a message and refreshes the displayed status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"When a buyer has no orders, My orders shows 'No orders yet' with a link to Find parts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"All three screens display without horizontal scrolling at viewport widths from 360px upward.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"Every form field has a visible label, and all controls are reachable and usable by keyboard alone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"With 5,000 parts in the database, Find parts loads its first page of results in under 2 seconds.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}